    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250-a2">

                <pb facs="0408" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg314"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1 in No. 441.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilkinson to the Commissioner of
                    Navigation.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port of New Orleans, La.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                                1896.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In the matter of incendiary fires on cotton
                    ships, referred to in your letter (14388–N) of May 5, 1896, a partial report in
                    relation to which was forwarded May 20. I have now the honor to transmit a
                    letter just received from the acting president of the New Orleans Cotton
                    Exchange, inclosing a report from the principal of the harbor protection police.
                    These communications, with the one previously forwarded will, I think, cover
                    fully the information requested by the Department to enable it to make a reply
                    to the State Department.</p>
                <p>No violations of section 4472, Revised Statutes, and section 8 of the “passenger
                    act of 1882,” have yet been reported to the United States attorney for
                    prosecution. The two cases cited by the British ambassador at Washington were of
                    vessels which carried freight exclusively, and which were therefore not amenable
                    to the provisions of the passenger act.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theo S. Wilkinson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
